  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The ionisation enthalpy increases as we go from left to right in a period, while it decreases as we come down a group. So&nbsp;according to this, the order will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>. But there are two exceptions, in the case of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> because of the highly stable&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;(completely filled orbital)&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;(half-filled orbital <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>)&nbsp;valence configuration. Due to this, the correct order is:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
